WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.210
Our staff wanted to move the

2
00:00:02.210 --> 00:00:03.630
start of the school day later.

3
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.460
Some said pupils would sleep

4
00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:08.240
more and learn better.

5
00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:10.960
Others worried about parents' work.

6
00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:13.900
How could data help us decide?

7
00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:18.340
Today: how a school can use data to decide

8
00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:20.940
well, and when data is not enough.

9
00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:24.900
Data cannot make a decision for you.

10
00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:26.980
It shows what is likely to

11
00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:28.320
happen and to whom.

12
00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:30.490
People still weigh what matters

13
00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:32.570
most, and they own the decision.

14
00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:37.290
We wrote one clear question: if we

15
00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:39.430
start thirty minutes later, will

16
00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:40.990
lateness and tiredness fall?

17
00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:44.330
Then we chose what to measure before

18
00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:47.030
collecting anything, so we could not pick

19
00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:48.750
the numbers we liked afterwards.

20
00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:52.550
Two classes started later for six weeks

21
00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:55.070
while two similar classes did not.

22
00:00:55.730 --> 00:00:57.870
Late arrivals per week fell from

23
00:00:57.870 --> 00:01:00.330
twelve to five in the trial classes,

24
00:01:00.770 --> 00:01:02.450
and barely changed in the others.

25
00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:05.850
Numbers were only half the story.

26
00:01:06.510 --> 00:01:08.190
We also asked parents and

27
00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:10.450
pupils, and some families could

28
00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:11.850
not manage the later finish.

29
00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:14.660
Their voices changed our plan

30
00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:16.300
more than any chart.

31
00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:19.220
Ms Farah shared the results with

32
00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:21.960
everyone, including what did not work.

33
00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:24.880
Now any teacher can bring a question

34
00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:26.380
to our monthly data meeting.

35
00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:29.560
Small honest trials have become

36
00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:30.780
how our school decides.

37
00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:32.850
Quick check!

38
00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:36.240
Why did we keep two similar classes on

39
00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:38.500
the old start time during the trial?

40
00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:40.940
To compare fairly.

41
00:01:41.770 --> 00:01:43.830
Lateness might have fallen anyway,

42
00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:45.970
because of the weather or the season.

43
00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:48.690
The other classes show what would

44
00:01:48.690 --> 00:01:50.250
have happened without the change.

45
00:01:51.580 --> 00:01:53.940
In the app, open the decision lab.

46
00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:56.580
Weigh the evidence and the voices

47
00:01:56.580 --> 00:01:59.140
for a school change, and see how

48
00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:00.720
your choice affects each group.

49
00:02:01.940 --> 00:02:02.480
Your turn.

50
00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:04.910
The data shows a later

51
00:02:04.910 --> 00:02:06.630
start cuts lateness.

52
00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:09.040
Who should make the final decision?

53
00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:12.760
The school's people, using the

54
00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:14.740
data and the voices together.

55
00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:19.300
Remember: ask one clear question, run

56
00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:22.200
a fair trial, listen as well as

57
00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:24.620
count, and share what you find.

58
00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:28.300
Try it with your staff this week: bring

59
00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:30.360
one school question to your next meeting

60
00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:32.340
and agree on what to measure.

61
00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:35.790
Then plan a small trial, with a similar

62
00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:38.250
group kept the same for a fair comparison.
